From afe4373d1d3ae209081879a79694f3d4d6a99227 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Portisch <hugo.portisch@yahoo.de>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:33:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] s3:libsmb: Limit the tree disconnect wait in cli_shutdown()

When the echo to a cached server times out, cli_shutdown() sends its
tree disconnect on the same dead connection and waits for the timeout
a second time. A client resuming from a suspend waits twice the
timeout per cached server, and other callers wait the same way.

Suggested-by: Ralph Boehme <slow@samba.org>
Signed-off-by: Portisch <hugo.portisch@yahoo.de>
---
 source3/libsmb/clientgen.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/source3/libsmb/clientgen.c b/source3/libsmb/clientgen.c
index 40da6d2..8c925d6 100644
--- a/source3/libsmb/clientgen.c
+++ b/source3/libsmb/clientgen.c
@@ -254,8 +254,12 @@ static void _cli_shutdown(struct cli_state *cli)
 	 * can remain active on the peer end, until some (long) timeout period
 	 * later.  This tree disconnect forces the peer to clean up, since the
 	 * connection will be going away.
+	 *
+	 * The peer may be gone already, for example after the client
+	 * resumed from a suspend, so don't wait longer than 1 second.
 	 */
 	if (cli_state_has_tcon(cli)) {
+		cli->timeout = MIN((cli->timeout ? cli->timeout : 1000), 1000);
 		cli_tdis(cli);
 	}
 
